rent folder name (e.g. it may be cloned as `godot-cpp.git`), and the `test` folder may not always be there in the future or include documentation.\r\n\r\nI think this would be better solved by improving the logic so it doesn't go so deep.\r\n\r\nThe patterns to support are:\r\n```\r\nmodules/<name>/doc_classes\r\nplatform/<name>/doc_classes\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo if we limit ourselves to one level of depth it should be fine I expect.\r\n\r\nOtherwise, adding a way to pass excludes from the command line might be better than hardcoding exceptions here.","created_at":"2025-06-12T14:34:56Z","updated_at":"2025-06-12T14:34:56Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103625#discussion_r2142943298","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103625","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2142943298"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/103625#discussion_r2142943298"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/103625"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2142943298/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":736,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2067461286,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":6,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2143803443","pull_request_review_id":2922869754,"id":2143803443,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc5_x9gz","diff_hunk":"@@ -731,6 +731,10 @@ def main() -> None:\n \n         if os.path.basename(path) in [\"modules\", \"platform\"]:\n             for subdir, dirs, _ in os.walk(path):\n+                # Exclude godot-cpp test project files for the case of\n+                # third-party modules with godot-cpp inside of them.\n+                